check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.4984725Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.4992307Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5085424Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5094417Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5095625Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5096321Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5096681Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5097036Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5097684Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5098090Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5098431Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5103144Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5103772Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5104341Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5105539Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5106569Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5107052Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5107407Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5107747Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5108184Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5108503Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5109084Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5109345Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5109495Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5109747Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5110188Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5111009Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5111445Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5111681Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5111882Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5112227Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5112756Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5113292Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5113948Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5114395Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5114772Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5115676Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5116267Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5121716Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5122507Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5131351Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5132160Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5132520Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5132853Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5133575Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5150635Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5151858Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5161460Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5162831Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5163387Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5163771Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5164051Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5164338Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5164655Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5165405Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5165753Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5165902Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5166329Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5166701Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5166997Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5167563Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5167780Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5167836Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5168318Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5171703Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:55:29.5172406Z been installed on this system.
